{"clock":1,"nonce":"3cb8222f8547a58acc3d62a828a3aee8","ops":[{"kind":"create","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792611702,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:5967331604"},"data":{"body":"Found cutting v0.9.0 (GB-19).\n\nA cut pushes the tag, then builds in a fresh `git worktree add --detach`. That checkout has no installed dependencies: no `web/node_modules`, no vendored tools. Two problems come from this:\n\n1. **Enable binary release infers a build that fails in a clean checkout.** For git-board it wrote `build = \"make dist\"`. `dist` depends on `web-build`, so the cut stops at `sh: quasar: command not found`. The Makefile's own comment says to run `cd web \u0026\u0026 npm ci` first. This repo's toml works around it with `build = \"(cd web \u0026\u0026 npm ci) \u0026\u0026 make dist\"`.\n2. **A build that fails leaves a pushed tag and no release.** The tag is pushed before `finish` → `binaries`. Does the next online cut or `reconcile` retry the build and publish for a pushed tag that has no record? If not, recovery is by hand.\n\nDone when:\n- the setup either infers the dependency install (a `package-lock.json` beside a Makefile target that builds the web, for example) or shows the build command for the user to confirm before Enable;\n- the setup check runs the build in a clean checkout before the first cut, or a failed build after the push is retried by the next cut or reconcile; a test covers whichever is chosen;\n- `docs/configuration.md` (Release) says the build runs in a clean checkout.","title":"release: a binary build that fails in the cut's clean checkout, after the tag is pushed"}},{"kind":"change-labels","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792611704,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:5967331604"},"data":{"add":["kind:bug","prio:p2","status:backlog","assignee:guilbep"],"remove":null}}]}